  "answer": "Project Zenith is an internal initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions with enhanced security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in July 2023 (Q3) with a focus on leveraging AI for data visualization and predictive analytics. Key milestones include a $2M budget approval, the addition of five new team members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, and upcoming updates to security protocols (MFA and encryption) effective January next year. The team is currently in Phase Two, having achieved breakthroughs in predictive analytics, with a detailed report scheduled for the November 20th staff meeting. Feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November, and partnership discussions with TechInnovate for AI technology are in early stages."
